# Flutter admin web — system notifications (orders, donations, refunds) — Cursor prompt

Implements **real-time operational alerts** for the CMS (Flutter Web admin panel), backed by:

- Backend: `docs/ADMIN_NOTIFICATIONS.md`, `GET/POST /api/v1/admin/notifications`, `POST /api/v1/fcm/register`
- Existing broadcast UI: `CmsNotificationsContent` + `GET /notifications` (manual push send/history) — **do not merge** with this feature.

Copy everything below the rule into Cursor inside **`Satya_devotte_app`** when extending or debugging. Match existing patterns: **GetX**, **Dio** + `ApiClient`, **CMS shell** hash routes, **FcmBootstrap** (web + mobile).

---

## Implementation status (Satya_devotte_app)

| Area | Status | Key files |
|------|--------|-----------|
| Activity inbox + API | Done | `features/admin_notifications/`, `CmsAdminNotificationsController`, `cms_admin_notifications_content.dart` |
| CMS bell + badge + polling | Done | `cms_shell_page.dart` |
| Web FCM register | Done | `fcm_bootstrap.dart` (`_registerWeb`, `platform: web`) |
| Web FCM routing | Done | `admin_notification_router.dart`, `push_router.dart`, `notification_service.dart` |
| VAPID | Required at build | `--dart-define=FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY=...` in `app_env.dart` |
| Service worker | Required | `web/firebase-messaging-sw.js` |

Backend must be deployed with `POST /fcm/register`, `GET /admin/notifications`, and payment verify hooks (see `docs/ADMIN_NOTIFICATIONS.md`). FCM `data` includes `notificationId` for mark-read on tap.

---

## What you are building

| Feature | API | UI |
|---------|-----|-----|
| **System alerts** (new order, donation paid, refund request) | `/admin/notifications` | Inbox + header bell badge |
| **Broadcast push** (admin composes message) | `/notifications/send` | Existing **Notifications** tab — leave as-is |

When a customer **pays** for an order or donation, every admin/superadmin with registered FCM tokens gets a push; history is stored server-side (not device-local).

---

## Backend contract (locked — do not change server)

Base: `${API_BASE_URL}/api/v1`  
Auth: `Authorization: Bearer <Firebase ID token>`  
Role: `admin` or `superadmin` only.

### FCM token (after CMS login)

```http
POST /fcm/register
{ "token": "<fcm_token>", "platform": "web", "deviceId": "web-<uuid>" }

DELETE /fcm/unregister
{ "token": "<fcm_token>" }

GET /fcm/me
→ { "count": 2, "devices": [...], "role": "admin" }
```

Register on login + `onTokenRefresh`. Unregister on logout (before clearing session). Multiple browser tabs = multiple tokens (expected).

### Admin inbox

| Method | Path |
|--------|------|
| `GET` | `/admin/notifications?page&limit&unreadOnly&type` |
| `GET` | `/admin/notifications/unread-count` |
| `GET` | `/admin/notifications/:id` |
| `POST` | `/admin/notifications/:id/read` |
| `POST` | `/admin/notifications/read-all` |

### List response

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "notifications": [
      {
        "id": "674a1b2c3d4e5f6789012345",
        "type": "NEW_ORDER",
        "title": "New order",
        "body": "Order SATYA-ORD-10042 — ZAR 299.00 from Jane",
        "data": {
          "type": "NEW_ORDER",
          "orderId": "674a...",
          "orderNumber": "SATYA-ORD-10042",
          "totalAmount": "299",
          "currency": "ZAR",
          "paystackReference": "T123"
        },
        "read": false,
        "createdAt": "2026-05-19T10:30:00.000Z"
      }
    ],
    "unreadCount": 3,
    "pagination": { "page": 1, "limit": 20, "total": 3, "totalPages": 1 }
  }
}
```

### Notification `type` values (FCM `data.type` matches)

| `type` | When fired | Navigate on tap |
|--------|------------|-----------------|
| `NEW_ORDER` | Order payment verified | Pooja Kit order detail |
| `PAYMENT_SUCCESS` | Donation payment verified (`data.paymentFor` = `DONATION`) | All Donations / contributions |
| `REFUND_REQUEST` | User opens refund request | Pooja Kit refunds |
| `REPLACEMENT_REQUEST` | User submits replacement | Pooja Kit refunds (or replacements if separate) |

### FCM payload example (`NEW_ORDER`)

```json
{
  "notification": { "title": "New order", "body": "Order SATYA-ORD-10042 — ZAR 299.00" },
  "data": {
    "type": "NEW_ORDER",
    "orderId": "674a1b2c3d4e5f6789012345",
    "orderNumber": "SATYA-ORD-10042",
    "userId": "674b...",
    "totalAmount": "299",
    "currency": "ZAR"
  }
}
```

### Curl (sanity check)

```bash
BASE="https://satya-server-app-2.onrender.com/api/v1"
TOKEN="<ADMIN_FIREBASE_JWT>"

curl -s "$BASE/admin/notifications/unread-count" -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
curl -s "$BASE/admin/notifications?unreadOnly=true" -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
```

---

## Web FCM checklist (admin CMS)

1. Firebase Console → Cloud Messaging → **Web Push certificates** → copy VAPID public key.
2. Run / build web with:
   ```bash
   flutter run -d chrome --dart-define=FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY=<your_vapid_public_key>
   ```
3. Confirm `web/firebase-messaging-sw.js` exists and matches your Firebase project.
4. Log in as admin → browser allows notifications → console: `[FCM] web token registered`.
5. `GET /api/v1/fcm/me` → `count` ≥ 1, `devices` includes `platform: web`.
6. Trigger test order/donation payment → tray notification + Activity row + badge increment.

**Foreground:** inbox refreshes; no auto-navigation (by design). **Tap:** `AdminNotificationRouter` → mark read + deep link.

**Still separate:** sidebar **Notifications** tab = manual broadcast (`POST /notifications/send`), not Activity.

---

## Recommended UX (CMS web)

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  CMS Shell                                    [🔔 3]   │
├──────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Sidebar  │  Activity inbox (or dropdown from bell)    │
│ …        │  • New order — SATYA-ORD-10042             │
│ Activity │  • Payment received — donation             │
│ Notif.*  │  • Refund request — REQ-1005               │
└──────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
* "Notifications" = existing broadcast send/history tab
```

**Option A (recommended):** New sidebar item **Activity** with unread badge.  
**Option B:** Bell opens `endDrawer` / overlay list; "View all" → full Activity page.

Implement **Option A + functional bell** (bell opens same inbox or scrolls to Activity tab).

